@*
    Audit Configuration flow (migration 276) -- Phase 1.

    Screen key : `org-audit-configuration`
    Group      : Audit Management
    Menu       : nav-assurance ("Audit Management") -> Audit Configuration
                 (a clickable parent: a real page AND the parent of the
                 five screens it hosts)

    How the audit operates, once it is defined:
        1. Evidence Configuration -> org-assurance-evidence-config
        2. Workflow Configuration -> org-assurance-workflow-config
        3. Scoring Configuration  -> org-assurance-scoring-config
        4. Trigger                -> org-assurance-triggers
        5. Scope Resolution       -> org-assurance-scope-resolution

    ORDER, AND WHY
      All five are keyed on (org_assurance_definition_id,
      org_assurance_definition_version_id), so they share one audit
      context and the first four are independent of each other -- the
      order is the BRD reading order (Sec 5, 6, 7, 9), not a dependency
      chain. Scope Resolution is last on purpose: it RESOLVES the scope
      authored in the Audit Definition flow into a snapshot, so it is
      the step that is meaningful only once the rest is in place. Its
      snapshots are immutable, which makes it the natural closing
      review step.

    ASSURANCE PLANS IS DELIBERATELY NOT A STEP HERE
      org_assurance_plan is organization-scoped and its items each
      reference a definition, so one plan spans several audits. Nesting
      it inside a per-audit stepper would invert that relationship, so
      it stays its own item under Audit Management.
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen
@{
    var flow = new AuditFlowShell(Model, "oaAuditConfigurationFlow",
    new AuditFlowStep[]
    {
        new AuditFlowStep(
            "evidence",
            "Evidence",
            "What evidence the audit collects, how it is collected, and what is mandatory.",
            "Partials/org-assurance-evidence-config"),
        new AuditFlowStep(
            "workflow",
            "Workflow",
            "The stages the audit moves through, who owns each one, and the SLA.",
            "Partials/org-assurance-workflow-config"),
        new AuditFlowStep(
            "scoring",
            "Scoring",
            "How results are scored: model type, thresholds and outcome bands.",
            "Partials/org-assurance-scoring-config"),
        new AuditFlowStep(
            "trigger",
            "Trigger",
            "What starts the audit -- a schedule, an event, a continuous source, or a person.",
            "Partials/org-assurance-triggers"),
        new AuditFlowStep(
            "scope-resolution",
            "Scope Resolution",
            "Resolve the authored scope into an immutable snapshot of the entities the audit will cover.",
            "Partials/org-assurance-scope-resolution")
    });
}

<partial name="Partials/_audit-flow-shell" model="flow" />
